# GLOBAL TEMPORARY FULL-SUITE POLICY — **ACTIVE / TEMPORARY**

Canonical document: `docs/governance/global-temporary-full-suite-policy.md`.
This rule is the durable mirror. Where they differ, the document governs.

**Status: ACTIVE.** Authorised by explicit user decision, effective 2026-08-19,
global across the current corrective/fix series. It **defers** one gate; it
removes none.

## The rule

1. **The Full Suite MUST NOT be run on an individual fix sprint** while this
   policy is ACTIVE. Do not recommend it, do not dispatch it, do not run a
   whole-repository `php artisan test` for a fix.
2. The Full Suite is **deferred**, never cancelled as a concept, to **one
   authoritative consolidated run on the frozen final integrated SHA** after all
   fixes are complete.
3. If you believe a specific change is risky enough to warrant a Full Suite:
   **state why and ask the user. Never run it automatically.** Only an explicit
   user override for that specific run permits it.

## What is still mandatory on every fix (unchanged)

Targeted tests · dependency-aware cumulative regression · security review ·
architecture review · `pint` · `git diff --check` · permission/module suites ·
**all required non-Full-Suite CI gates** (NSF-R012 Quality, CICD-CTRL
Classifier, NSF-R011 Critical, CICD-CTRL Selective Module, NSF-9 Release Safety
& Smoke, NSF-10 Release Evidence) · merge verification · deploy verification ·
production smoke · rules sync · cleanup.

> "Full Suite skipped, therefore other tests may be skipped" is **forbidden
> reasoning**. This policy narrows exactly one gate.

Regression is **risk-based and dependency-based** — derive it from
`sprint:test-plan` + `graphify`, not by running the whole repository and not by
running too little.

## The local trigger inside DEVFLOW — read this first

**`php artisan sprint:test --all-required` (and `--regression`) runs the FULL
SUITE** — it appends a `pest-full-required` step of bare `php artisan test`
whenever `escalate_full_suite` is true, and escalation is **fail-closed** (an
unmatched changed file sets it; a sprint manifest matches nothing). **While this
policy is ACTIVE, do not run `--all-required` or `--regression`.** Use:

```bash
php artisan sprint:test-plan          # read-only
php artisan sprint:test --focused     # never escalates
vendor/bin/pint --dirty --test
git diff --check
php artisan test --filter='<targeted regression>'
```

This supersedes the "run `sprint:test --all-required` before release" line in
`docs/engineering/sprint-runtime-template.md`.

## Accidental triggers — know the mechanics

`full_suite_gate` fires on exactly three events:

- `pull_request` → **never fires**. A fix sprint's own PR is structurally
  `FULL_SUITE_EXECUTION_COUNT = 0`.
- `push` to the base branch → **fires**, and a squash-merge is such a push.
- `schedule` (weekly) → **fires**; calendar-driven, attributable to no sprint.
- `workflow_dispatch` + `run_full_suite=true` → **deliberate; forbidden while
  ACTIVE** except for the consolidated closure or an explicit user override.

`.sprint/current.yml` matches no classifier pattern → `unknown_high_risk`, so
every real sprint (which updates its manifest) enables the post-merge Full Suite
step. Only a genuinely docs-only change set resolves to `docs_only`.

Always resolve the profile with the real tool before pushing:
`scripts/ci/resolve-gates.sh --base origin/<base> --head HEAD`.

**Never** add `paths-ignore`, widen `skip_critical_profiles` beyond `docs_only`,
edit CI merely to hide a failure or force a skip, or manufacture a fake
docs-only change to obtain a weaker profile.

## Cancelling a post-merge run — permitted only under proof

An official `gh run cancel` of the push-to-base run is permitted **only** when
all hold: the pre-merge candidate was green on an identical tree; the cancel
lands **before the Full Suite job begins executing tests**; the run ID and the
`startedAt == completedAt` zero-duration proof are recorded; no CI file is
touched.

**Forbidden:** cancelling a Full Suite that has **already begun executing** in
order to make the count look like zero. That is an execution — record it, report
the partial result, never claim "never executed". Never cancel a *scheduled* run
for count management.

## Evidence — truthful or nothing

Every sprint report under this policy must carry:

```
FULL_SUITE_STATUS = SKIPPED_BY_GLOBAL_TEMPORARY_POLICY
FULL_SUITE_EXECUTION_COUNT = 0
GLOBAL_TEMPORARY_FULL_SUITE_POLICY_ACTIVE = YES
```

Never write `FULL SUITE PASS` if it did not run. **Job skipped ≠ tests passed.
Job cancelled ≠ tests passed. And `success` ≠ tests passed** — verified: on a
docs-only push to base the `NSF-R011 Full Suite Gate` job is **green while the
suite never ran** (`Run full Pest suite` = `skipped`, a "Note skipped full suite"
step writes the evidence). Read the **step**, never the job:

```bash
gh run view <run-id> --json jobs \
  --jq '.jobs[]|select(.name=="NSF-R011 Full Suite Gate")|.steps[]
        |select(.name|test("full Pest suite"))|"\(.conclusion)\t\(.name)"'
``` If an accidental Full Suite genuinely runs,
record run ID / SHA / event / result, report the breach, and never rewrite
history to protect a count.

## Closing posture and GO tags

A completed fix closes at **`WATCH — PENDING CONSOLIDATED FULL SUITE`** — it is
not failed and not unfinished. Distinguish **implementation closure** (reached)
from **final integrated verification closure** (deferred).

**No final engineering GO tag** for a fix whose governance requires a Full Suite
before GO. Never tag on a pretended pass. Historical GO tags and CI evidence are
**immutable** — never delete, move, downgrade, or rewrite them; this policy is
prospective only.

## Consolidated closure (do not start automatically)

Begins only when the user says all fixes are finished or authorises the final
Full Suite: inventory WATCH sprints → verify merged+deployed → freeze the final
integrated SHA → baseline re-verify → **one** authoritative Full Suite (expected
failures **0**) → production smoke → governance audit → GO decision → tags.

On failure: **NO FINAL GO**; record the exact failure set; **do not immediately
rerun**; diagnose with targeted tests; fix; merge/deploy; agree the next
authoritative run with the user. Never loop the Full Suite while debugging.

## Unchanged by this policy

Deployment (`bash scripts/deploy-vps-runner.sh start` **on the VPS**, real
`exit=0` + `DEPLOY OK`, backup first, `migrate --force` only, never
`migrate:fresh`/`db:wipe`) · production smoke over `https://daengtisia.online` ·
Legacy RME fail-closed / RM-derived branch authority / read-only archive / maker
≠ publisher / creator ≠ approver / admission EMPTY + capability OFF at rest ·
CICD-CTRL-1 default-strong classification · branch isolation · ledger-only
inventory · RBAC 3-layer · PII masking · additive-only migrations.

**This policy changes test scheduling only.**

## Retirement

Ends only on explicit user revocation, or on completed consolidated closure. One
finished fix does not end it. On retirement mark this rule and the canonical
document `RETIRED after consolidated Full Suite closure` — **never delete them.**

